# WF-007 – Escalation Engine

**Document ID:** WF-007

**Title:** Escalation Engine Specification

**Version:** 1.0

**Status:** Draft

**Owner:** S2PNexus Architecture Team

---

# 1. Purpose

The Escalation Engine manages overdue workflow tasks and SLA violations.

It ensures work progresses according to business policies while maintaining a complete audit trail.

The Escalation Engine is a shared platform capability used across Procurement, Supplier Management, Sourcing, Contracts, AP, AR, and all future S2PNexus modules.

---

# 2. Design Principles

The Escalation Engine shall be

- Policy Driven
- Metadata Driven
- Business Calendar Aware
- Time Zone Aware
- Multi-Tenant
- Configurable
- Auditable
- Event Driven
- AI Assisted

---

# 3. Architecture

```
Workflow Runtime

        │

        ▼

Escalation Engine

        │

┌──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬────────────┐

▼          ▼          ▼          ▼

Policy     SLA      Calendar     AI

        │

        ▼

Escalation Decision

        │

        ▼

Action Execution
```

---

# 4. Escalation Lifecycle

```
Task Assigned

↓

Monitor SLA

↓

Threshold Reached

↓

Evaluate Policy

↓

Determine Action

↓

Execute Action

↓

Audit & Notify

↓

Continue Monitoring (if applicable)
```

---

# 5. Escalation Triggers

Supported triggers

- SLA warning threshold
- SLA breach
- No acknowledgement
- No activity
- Timer expiration
- Manual escalation
- Business event
- Risk score increase
- AI recommendation

---

# 6. Escalation Levels

Example

```
Level 0  Assigned User

↓

Level 1  Supervisor

↓

Level 2  Manager

↓

Level 3  Director

↓

Level 4  Vice President

↓

Level 5  Executive

↓

Maximum Escalation Reached
```

Each level may define different actions.

---

# 7. Escalation Actions

Supported actions

- Reminder
- Re-notify
- Escalate
- Reassign
- Add watcher
- Increase priority
- Extend SLA
- Pause SLA
- Auto approve
- Auto reject
- Cancel task
- Create child workflow
- Create incident
- Invoke webhook
- Execute AI review

Multiple actions may be configured per level.

---

# 8. Business Calendar Support

Escalations honor

- Working days
- Business hours
- Holidays
- Country calendars
- Plant calendars
- Time zones
- Shift schedules

Example

```
Assigned Friday 5:00 PM

2 Business Days

↓

Due Tuesday 5:00 PM
```

---

# 9. Reminder Schedule

Reminder policies support

- One-time reminder
- Recurring reminder
- Progressive reminder
- Custom intervals
- Business-hour only reminders

Example

```
Day 1

↓

Reminder

↓

Day 2

↓

Reminder

↓

Day 3

↓

Escalate
```

---

# 10. Escalation Policy

Policy determines

- Trigger
- Threshold
- Escalation path
- Actions
- Stop conditions
- Notification channels

Policies are versioned and reusable.

---

# 11. Escalation Path Resolution

Resolution sources

- Organization hierarchy
- Delegation
- Business object owner
- Cost center owner
- Project manager
- Commodity manager
- Queue owner
- Static user
- AI recommendation

---

# 12. Stop Conditions

Escalation immediately stops when

- Task completed
- Task cancelled
- Workflow completed
- Workflow cancelled
- Task reassigned outside escalation scope
- Manual intervention resolves issue
- Maximum escalation level reached
- Maximum escalation duration exceeded
- Policy explicitly terminates escalation

---

# 13. Escalation Ceiling

Every policy may define

- Maximum level
- Maximum duration
- Maximum reminder count
- Maximum notifications
- Escalation ceiling role or group

Example

```
Assigned User

↓

Supervisor

↓

Manager

↓

Director

↓

STOP
```

---

# 14. Automatic Resolution

Escalation may automatically

- Close reminder chain
- Remove pending timers
- Cancel scheduled notifications
- Reset escalation counters
- Record completion metrics

---

# 15. AI-Assisted Escalation

AI may recommend

- Escalate earlier
- Delay escalation
- Change assignee
- Add reviewers
- Increase priority
- Predict SLA breach
- Recommend additional stakeholders

AI recommendations require configurable confidence thresholds and may require human approval.

---

# 16. Notification Integration

Supported channels

- Email
- SMS
- Microsoft Teams
- Slack
- Mobile Push
- Webhook

Notifications include

- Escalation level
- Reason
- Due date
- Current assignee
- Recommended action

---

# 17. Metrics

Collected metrics

- Escalations by workflow
- Escalations by user
- Average escalation level
- Average resolution time
- SLA breaches
- Reminder effectiveness
- Auto-resolution rate

---

# 18. Security

Escalation enforces

- Tenant isolation
- RBAC
- ABAC
- Segregation of Duties
- Audit logging

Only authorized users may override or terminate an escalation.

---

# 19. Audit

Every escalation event records

- Workflow instance
- Task instance
- Previous assignee
- New assignee
- Escalation level
- Policy applied
- Trigger
- Action executed
- Timestamp
- Correlation ID

